    },
    {
      "text": "Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Cook elbow macaroni in boiling water, stirring occasionally, until tender yet firm to the bite, about 8 minutes. Drain and rinse under cold running water.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir together macaroni, peas, celery, tuna, and onion in a large bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Wa8HLtiaLRsFsyDyd5Oq51cfWuc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/70208_AmeliasTunaMacaroniSalad_ddmfs_step2_4x3_2307-183367b7e0cd4fe6b3d56a1eaa9d47d4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/70208/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix in mayonnaise, relish, salt and pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/YNB_o8dlvyRuvqQ75JLrWQg4820=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/70208_AmeliasTunaMacaroniSalad_ddmfs_step3_4x3_2311-8b341c7159964d069854c67e4a036021.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/70208/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Garnish with egg wedges and a sprinkle of paprika. Cover and chill for at least 1 hour before serving.",
